# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0

config MESHTASTIC_WATCHDOG
	bool "Hardware watchdog (force-reset a wedged system)"
	default y
	select WATCHDOG
	help
	  Arms the SoC's hardware watchdog timer (wdt0) at boot and feeds it
	  periodically, but ONLY while meshtastic_watchdog_checkin() keeps landing
	  (wired to meshtastic_powermon_set(), which fires on every LoRa TX/RX
	  power-state transition — driven both by real RF activity and by the
	  unconditional periodic AGC-reset timer, so it ticks at least once every
	  CONFIG_MESHTASTIC_AGC_RESET_INTERVAL_MS regardless of mesh traffic).

	  This exists for a specific, observed gap: every silent-hang outage seen
	  on the bench (a node goes dark with zero log activity, no assert, no
	  fatal-error trace, unresponsive to ping/telnet/SMP) left NOTHING for
	  CONFIG_DEBUG_COREDUMP/CONFIG_RESET_ON_FATAL_ERROR to catch, because
	  those only fire on a software fault Zephyr's own detection can see (a
	  CPU exception, an assert, a stack overflow). A watchdog doesn't care
	  *why* the radio-power-state machine stopped ticking, only that it did —
	  so it catches the class of hang nothing else here can, at the cost of
	  turning "dead until someone finds it and power-cycles it" into
	  "auto-recovers within one timeout window."

if MESHTASTIC_WATCHDOG

config MESHTASTIC_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT_MS
	int "Watchdog timeout (ms)"
	default 180000
	range 60000 600000
	help
	  How long without a check-in before the hardware forces a reset. Set
	  generously above the guaranteed once-per-AGC-reset-interval tick
	  (default 60 s) to leave real margin for scheduling jitter, PM
	  light-sleep wake latency, or a legitimately slow admin/OTA operation —
	  this is a last-resort backstop, not a tight liveness probe.

config MESHTASTIC_WATCHDOG_FEED_INTERVAL_MS
	int "Watchdog feed-check interval (ms)"
	default 30000
	range 5000 60000
	help
	  How often the feed worker wakes up to decide whether to feed the
	  watchdog. Must be well under the timeout (several checks per window)
	  so a hang is caught within roughly one timeout period, not two.

endif # MESHTASTIC_WATCHDOG
